# anchor-stock — what stays out of a PRIVATE repository.
#
# The list is short on purpose. This repository is private (D-29), so nothing is excluded to
# keep it from readers — only things that are regenerable, machine-local, or actually secret.
# In particular `docs/` is TRACKED here, which is the point of D-29 and the reverse of what
# D-23/D-28 arranged in the public repository this one supersedes.
#
# Nothing here hides a source file. If a path is missing from a clone, it is because it can be
# rebuilt, not because it was withheld — which is exactly the property the previous arrangement
# could not offer.

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# .env.example is tracked and carries the variable NAMES with no values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Node / Next -----------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.next/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Regenerable data ------------------------------------------------------
# raw/ is provider payloads exactly as received; processed/ is typed parquet. Both are rebuilt
# by docs/RUNBOOK.md §3. reference/ and artifacts/ are deliberately NOT ignored: the sector map
# is curated by hand and the artifact is a frozen parameter set the dashboard actually serves.
data/raw/
data/processed/

# --- Machine-local ---------------------------------------------------------
.scratch/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
/reference